// The Default universe for the Open Universe - one authored file holding the
// whole world: identity (the level-1 heading), its clans, the generic clan jobs
// they offer, and the shared narrative arcs. Heading level sets structure:
//   #   the universe (identity + reputation rules)
//   ##  a section: Clans / Jobs / Narrative
//   ### an entry within a section (a clan, a job type, a narrative step)
// Each heading's data lives between `---` fences as friendly `Label: value` fact
// lines (no YAML). Lists use commas; weights are `name N`; makeup is `N% Race`;
// reputation axes are `pos / neg`; quest triggers are an English verb phrase.

# Default
---
Display: Default
// Reputation axes (per-captain spectrums). Authoring any Axis lines REPLACES the
// built-in set, so a different universe can carry its own axes (e.g. pious /
// heretical). Each axis is `positive / opposite`; drop the opposite for a single
// pole. Omit all reputation lines to use the built-in seven + default tuning.
Axis: honest / liar
Axis: fearsome / cowardly
Axis: peaceful / violent
Axis: generous / selfish
Axis: kind / cruel
Axis: resourceful / by-the-book
Axis: intellectual / foolish
Job tiers: 20, 50
Foe deals at: 20
Max reward: 2.0
Ceasefire free at: 30
Ceasefire per point: 20
Alliance at: 60
---
A living frontier of clans, trade, reputation, and contestable space docks. The
galaxy reacts to who you are, not to a scripted hero.

## Clans

The factions that hold this galaxy. Each heading key is the clan's side key; the
fact sheet sets identity + home systems; the prose is the description. Spawned as
sides by universe_clans.py.

Flies = the race composition of a clan's ships: a single race (Torgoth), an even
list (Torgoth, Kralien), or weighted (60% Kralien, 40% Arvonian). Omit for a
random mix. Races: Kralien, Torgoth, Arvonian, Ximni.

### Iron Concord (iron)
---
Color: #3399ff
Archetype: military
Disposition: neutral
Home: 6, 4
Values: by-the-book 40, fearsome 30, honest 20
Offers: patrol, escort, strike
Flies: 60% Kralien, 40% Arvonian
---
Disciplined and territorial. Respects strength and straight dealing; honor a deal
and the Concord remembers - break one and they remember longer.

### Verdant Pact (verdant)
---
Color: #44cc88
Archetype: trader
Disposition: neutral
Home: -5, 3
Values: peaceful 40, generous 30, kind 20
Offers: supply, escort, survey
Flies: Arvonian
---
Green-world traders and farmers. Quick to deal, slow to fight; pay them in
kindness and they pay you back in goods.

### Free Holders (free)
---
Color: #bb8855
Archetype: settler
Disposition: neutral
Home: -7, -7
Values: resourceful 40, honest 30, kind 10
Offers: salvage, rescue, supply
Flies: Kralien, Torgoth, Arvonian, Ximni
---
Independent settlers scratching a living from the drift. Self-reliant and plain-
spoken; they value a captain who gets things done.

### Mercury Guild (mercury)
---
Color: #ffbb00
Archetype: mercenary
Disposition: neutral
Home: 5, -3
Values: resourceful 30, selfish 30, fearsome 20
Offers: bounty, escort, smuggle
Flies: 40% Ximni, 30% Torgoth, 30% Kralien
---
Brokers of muscle and cargo - loyal to the contract, not the cause. Coin and a
fearsome reputation open their doors.

### Ashfang Raiders (ashfang)
---
Color: #ee3333
Archetype: pirate
Disposition: foe
Home: 8, -5
Values: violent 40, cruel 30, cowardly 20
Offers: raid, smuggle, bounty
Flies: Torgoth
---
Opportunist pirates who prey on the lanes. They respect violence and despise the
weak; only the dangerous bargain with them.

### Hollow Choir (choir)
---
Color: #9933ff
Archetype: cult
Disposition: foe
Home: -4, 6
Values: intellectual 40, liar 30, selfish 20
Offers: retrieve, escort, mystery
Flies: Ximni
---
A secretive cult chasing forbidden knowledge in the deep dark. Honeyed words hide
sharp intent; trust them at your peril.

## Jobs

Generic clan jobs. Each heading key is a pool type (see a clan's Offers); a clan
offers the jobs whose type is in its pool, gated + reward-scaled by the captain's
standing (universe_clan_quests.py). Goal is an English verb phrase that both sets
the trigger and reads as the objective: destroy / recover / scan / dock / reach.

### Patrol Sweep (patrol)
---
Tier: 1
Goal: destroy 4 raiders
Pays: 300 credits
---
Raiders have been probing our space. Sweep the system and drive them off.

### Standing Bounty (bounty)
---
Tier: 1
Goal: destroy 3 raiders
Pays: 280 credits
---
There is a price on raider hulls. Collect three and the bounty is yours.

### Supply Run (supply)
---
Tier: 1
Goal: recover 3 provisions
Pays: 260 credits
---
Our stores are thin. Gather provision crates adrift in the system and bring
them in.

### Survey Contract (survey)
---
Tier: 1
Goal: scan 2 derelicts
Pays: 300 credits
---
We need eyes on the wrecks out here. Scan the derelicts and report what you find.

### Salvage Sweep (salvage)
---
Tier: 1
Goal: recover 2 tech
Pays: 340 credits
---
There is working tech in the debris if you know where to look. Bring it back and
we will make it worth your while.

### Convoy Escort (escort)
---
Tier: 1
Goal: dock station
Pays: 260 credits
---
See our cargo safely to port. Dock at a station and the contract is fulfilled.

### Run the Lanes (smuggle)
---
Tier: 2
Goal: recover 2 contraband
Pays: 480 credits
---
Quiet cargo, quiet questions. Recover the caches and keep this between us.

### Raid the Lanes (raid)
---
Tier: 2
Goal: destroy 5 raiders
Pays: 500 credits
---
Hit them before they hit us. Five hulls, and do not be gentle about it.

### Retrieve the Cache (retrieve)
---
Tier: 2
Goal: recover 3 tech
Pays: 520 credits
---
Something we want is scattered in the drift. Retrieve three components - discreetly.

### Search and Rescue (rescue)
---
Tier: 2
Goal: scan 1 derelict
Pays: 460 credits
---
A ship went dark out here. Find the wreck, recover what survives, and bring it home.

### Strike Package (strike)
---
Tier: 3
Goal: destroy 8 raiders
Pays: 760 credits
---
We are done waiting. Take the fight to them - eight hulls, and break their nerve.

### Chase the Whisper (mystery)
---
Tier: 3
Goal: scan 3 derelicts
Pays: 720 credits
---
The signs are out there for those who would read them. Scan the wrecks. Tell no
one what you see.

## Narrative

Shared story arcs - game-wide reveal chains spanning systems. Each heading is one
step; the fact sheet sets scope (shared), starting state (active now / secret =
revealed later), the trigger (When), the next step (Then: reveal ...), and any
reward (Pays / Earns). Granted at universe start via quest_grant_amd.

### The Long Truce: Summons (truce_1)
---
Scope: shared
State: active
When: reach 6, 4
Then: reveal truce_2
---
A coded hail from Iron Concord HQ at system (6, 4). Travel there to hear them out.

### The Long Truce: Proof of Resolve (truce_2)
---
Scope: shared
State: secret
When: destroy 3 ashfang
Then: reveal truce_3
Pays: 100 credits
---
The Concord wants a broker for a ceasefire with the Ashfang Raiders. Thin the
raiders - destroy three - to show the Concord you can hold the line.

### The Long Truce: The Accord (truce_3)
---
Scope: shared
State: secret
When: dock station
Pays: 800 credits
Earns: iron honest 20, iron fearsome 10
---
Return to a Concord starbase to seal the accord.
